#: ../../source/references_effects.md:737
msgid "Effect Nodes — Uniform Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:739
msgid ""
"In the v2 protocol, effect nodes are used **inside** scene functions. The"
" scene function itself returns a canvas. Effect nodes produce "
"intermediate `(chars, colors)` that are rendered to canvas via the grid's"
" `.render()` method or `_render_vf()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:759
msgid "Value Field Generators (Atomic Building Blocks)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:761
msgid ""
"These produce float32 arrays `(rows, cols)` in range [0,1]. They are the "
"raw visual patterns. All have signature `(g, f, t, S, **params) -> "
"float32 array`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:763
msgid "Trigonometric Fields (sine/cosine-based)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:869
msgid "Noise-Based Fields (organic, non-periodic)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:871
msgid ""
"These produce qualitatively different textures from sine-based fields — "
"organic, non-repeating, without visible axis alignment. They're the "
"foundation of high-end generative art."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1022
msgid "Simulation-Based Fields (emergent, evolving)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1024
msgid ""
"These use persistent state `S` to evolve patterns frame-by-frame. They "
"produce complexity that can't be achieved with stateless math."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1231
msgid "SDF-Based Fields (geometric precision)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1233
msgid ""
"Signed Distance Fields produce mathematically precise shapes. Unlike sine"
" fields (organic, blurry), SDFs give hard geometric boundaries with "
"controllable edge softness. Combined with domain warping, they create "
"\"melting geometry\" effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1235
msgid ""
"All SDF primitives return a **signed distance** (negative inside, "
"positive outside). Convert to a value field with `sdf_render()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1371
msgid "Hue Field Generators (Color Mapping)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_effects.md:1373
msgid ""
"These produce float32 hue arrays [0,1]. Independently combinable with any"
" value field. Each is a factory returning a closure with signature `(g, "
"f, t, S) -> float32 array`. Can also be a plain float for fixed hue."
msgstr ""

